<title>NORWAY: Bergesen Q1 operating profit rises 21 pct.</title>
<headline>Bergesen Q1 operating profit rises 21 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to March 31.</p>
<p>				   (millions of crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Operating revenue		  1,259     vs	1,209</p>
<p> Operating profit		     228     vs	  189</p>
<p> After-tax profit		     185     vs	  221</p>
<p>NOTE -- Full name of Norway's largest shipping company is Bergesen d.y. Group ASA. A Reuter poll of nine analysts forecast a first-quarter operating result of 184 million crowns and after-tax profits of 117 million crowns.  </p>
<p> Operating expenses		   859     vs	  846</p>
<p> Depreciation		   minus 172     vs  minus 174</p>
<p> Profit on sale of securities	-	vs	    7</p>
<p> Foreign exchange income    minus  27     vs	   29</p>
<p> Net interest expenses		 65     vs	   70</p>
<p> Other financial items net  minus   1     vs  minus   5</p>
<p>Profit/loss on sale of</p>
<p>	   long-term assets	    50     vs	   10</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit			 185     vs	  221</p>
<p> Tax					 -	vs	   -</p>
<p>NOTE -- Bergesen said the 1996 figures had been adjusted to for the new accounting principle for drydocking expenses and the change in deferred tax due to the new tax regime for Norwegian shipping.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
